# Astra Pro audit bundle: CM/ANF optimization experiments N1, P1-P13

Prepared 2026-09-18 for an independent adversarial audit before any P14 implementation is frozen.

## Why this bundle exists

This package is intended to let Astra Pro reconstruct the P1-P13 optimization campaign from primary artifacts rather than from chat summaries. The audit question is not merely "did P13 get faster?" but:

- what transformation is actually being performed;
- whether the direct/no-rewrite baseline is fair;
- why propagated two-support information reduces sparse-ANF work;
- which costs are algorithmic versus CPython/runtime artifacts;
- whether P1-P13 measurement and statistics support the interpretations made so far;
- whether a pure-Python cleanup or a different experiment should precede a compiled P14;
- and, if compiled code is the right next step, how to design P14 without creating a compiled-vs-Python fairness artifact.

**Start with `01_PROMPT/ASTRA_PRO_P1_P13_AUDIT_PROMPT.md`.**

Astra should inspect source code, preregistrations and raw result files before relying on `*_RESULTS.md` or `*_INTERPRETATION.md`.

